rules:
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture decisions must be recorded and updated only in decision records
    (ADR); all other representations must be derived from ADR.
  title: ADR as Single Source of Truth
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The AEM must remain consistent with ADR decisions and never contradict
    them, while it may include vision, roadmap, system evolution, and architectural
    direction.
  title: AEM Consistency with Decisions
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source for architectural planning
    state; generated artifacts must derive planning status from Architecture Work
    rather than maintain independent planning state.
  title: Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns must represent foundational architectural primitives, not
    specific strategies or implementations.
  title: Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All ADR decisions must use the structured YAML decision schema rather than
    unstructured narrative, separating architect decision status from governance approval.
  title: Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Lifecycle stage must be derived from decision status: proposed maps to
    NEXT or REVIEW, accepted may map to DONE, rejected must not appear active, and
    deferred maps to FUTURE or DEFER.'
  title: Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be persisted as structured ADR records
    before being reflected in AEM or other artifacts.
  title: Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Patterns must not be merged or consolidated across different architectural
    layers.
  title: Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts must summarize authoritative sources and
    must not become authoritative sources themselves.
  title: Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must include at least one linked signal
    as evidence.
  title: Heuristic-Derived Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Foundational global semantic contract that distinguishes intent, decision,
    and system state, and enforces consistent lifecycle terminology across architecture
    artifacts.
  title: Language & Semantics Contract
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern maturity and decision lifecycle are distinct but must be interpreted
    consistently, with decision status controlling AEM stage assignment.
  title: Pattern and Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All patterns must be created as supporting by default and never directly
    as core.
  title: Patterns Must Be Created as Supporting
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Global rules override project rules and prompt rules; conflicts must be
    detected, resolved by precedence, and surfaced in governance artifacts.
  title: Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core must be supported by strong evidence, preferably
    from multiple sources or systems.
  title: Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects participate in a shared Knowledge Workspace and must not duplicate
    existing workspace-level governance structures when an available workspace exists.
  title: Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: A signal may be promoted to a pattern only when recurrence, system impact,
    reusability, stability, and supporting evidence are all satisfied.
  title: Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The system proposes architectural decisions, and an architect must explicitly
    accept, reject, or defer each decision.
  title: System Proposes, Architect Decides
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Runtime-native workflows must comply with the CAS Workflow Execution Model,
    where CAS Runner orchestrates, workflows reason, knowledge providers access knowledge,
    and outputs conform to declared schemas.
  title: Workflow Execution Model Compliance
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
